/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL007 -- Non-Newtonian Flow in a Pipe
  (Ansys Fluid Dynamics Verification Manual, Release 2026 R1, printed p. 29).

  The archive is 2D AXISYMMETRIC -- verified in the archive's own settings blob,
  `(rp-axi? . #t)` and `(rp-3d? . #f)`, with a zone literally named `axis`.  The
  OpenFOAM analogue is a single-cell-thick `wedge`.

  Pipe axis is +x, 0 <= x <= L = 0.1 m.  R = D/2 = 0.00125 m.

  WEDGE TOTAL ANGLE t = 1 deg, HALF-ANGLE 0.5 deg.  Wall vertices sit at EXACT
  radius R:  y_w = R cos(0.5 deg), z_w = +/- R sin(0.5 deg), so |(y_w,z_w)| = R
  to machine precision (NOT y = R, z = R tan a, which puts the wall at R/cos a).

  WHY 1 deg AND NOT THE TEAM'S 5 deg (VMFL003/VMFL005) -- this is N-AV9's OWN
  NAMED MITIGATION, taken deliberately and with a stated criterion:
      t = 5 deg : dp biased HIGH by sec(2.5 deg) - 1 = +0.09526851633199218 %
      t = 1 deg : dp biased HIGH by sec(0.5 deg) - 1 = +0.003807838573699485 %
  The manual prints its target to four figures (60.52 kPa), so the reference is
  itself known only to +/- 5 Pa = +/- 0.00826 %.  THE CRITERION APPLIED HERE:
  the wedge modelling bias must sit BELOW the reference's own rounding
  half-width, so that a bias no refinement can remove is also a bias the
  reference cannot resolve.  1 deg satisfies it (0.00381 % < 0.00826 %); 5 deg
  misses it by 11.5x.

  N-AV9 / CHARTER v1.4 CLAUSE A -- THE BIAS IS AZIMUTHAL AND NO REFINEMENT
  REMOVES IT.  For a PRESSURE-DROP gate the governing term is sec(t/2) - 1, the
  RATIO of the wall-arc deficit to the area deficit, NOT the sin(t)/t area
  deficit on its own.  From the fully developed force balance dp*A = tau_w*P*L:
      true circular sector  P/A = 2/R
      flat-sided wedge      P/A = 2/(R cos(t/2))
      ratio                 = sec(t/2)                 <-- dp biased HIGH
  At t = 1 deg:  area ratio sin(t)/t   = 0.9999492312032947 (deficit 0.005076879670529166 %)
                 arc  ratio sin(t/2)/(t/2) = 0.9999873076558379 (deficit 0.001269234416212406 %)
                 dp bias  sec(t/2) - 1 = 3.807838573699485e-05 = +0.003807838573699485 %
  Carried in PREREGISTRATION.md section 6 (error budget) with its SIGN.

  __NX__  axial cells (x)
  __NR__  radial cells (r), UNIFORM.  There is NO wall function in this case --
          it is LAMINAR -- so N-AV10's axial-only constraint DOES NOT APPLY and
          the Roache triple refines RADIALLY as well as axially.
  Substituted by run_vmfl007.sh; this template is never edited by a run.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object blockMeshDict; }

mergeType points;   // wedge geometry -- merge the coincident axis points

scale   1;

vertices
(
    (0.0  0                       0                      )   // 0  inlet  axis
    (0.1  0                       0                      )   // 1  outlet axis
    (0.0  0.0012499524038302142  -1.0908169372967418e-05 )   // 2  inlet  wall back  (z<0)
    (0.1  0.0012499524038302142  -1.0908169372967418e-05 )   // 3  outlet wall back
    (0.0  0.0012499524038302142   1.0908169372967418e-05 )   // 4  inlet  wall front (z>0)
    (0.1  0.0012499524038302142   1.0908169372967418e-05 )   // 5  outlet wall front
);

blocks
(
    hex (0 1 3 2  0 1 5 4) (__NX__ __NR__ 1) simpleGrading (1 1 1)
);

edges ( );

boundary
(
    inlet  { type patch; faces ( (0 2 4 0) ); }
    outlet { type patch; faces ( (1 3 5 1) ); }
    walls  { type wall;  faces ( (2 3 5 4) ); }
    wedge1 { type wedge; faces ( (0 2 3 1) ); }
    wedge2 { type wedge; faces ( (0 1 5 4) ); }
);

mergePatchPairs ( );
